 "note": "One long snake from home to home (half-turn symmetry): three runs folded by hairpins (a Wide 90 and a 90 with a deck between), S-bends 2 / 4 m between half bridges along every run. Retract shortcuts cut across the folds: the centre relay drops both bridges to the far runs, the run-end relays drop the jumps onto the middle run. A flex S-bridge gives each home its back door.",
 "geometricSymmetry": true,
 "labVariant": {
  "junctions": true
 },
 "experimental": true,
 "ruleWaivers": {
  "S03": "half-turn symmetry: the front door (camera side) is the same for both seats, so the sim walk from each home differs by a few seconds - the same as the live point-symmetric pool maps N-11 / N-14 / N-20 / N-22 / N-24 / N-28 (first measured 2026-10-28, junction fairness walk); pending Daniele",
  "S04": "half-turn symmetry: the front door (camera side) is the same for both seats, so the sim walk from each home differs by a few seconds - the same as the live point-symmetric pool maps N-11 / N-14 / N-20 / N-22 / N-24 / N-28 (first measured 2026-10-28, junction fairness walk); pending Daniele",
  "N16": "the run-end relays drop their one jump onto the middle run - the serpent's idea; a second deck would be the home road (N04) or the rail (N05); pending Daniele"
 },
